YOUR TASK: Complete this task: Implement a standalone brute-force oracle and theorem validator for small cases: generate random/targeted instances with N<=10, M<=8, unique (S,T), |S-T|>1; for every subset, check feasibility by Bellman-Ford positive-cycle detection on prefix-sum difference constraints (0-weight equality l_i=r_i, 1-weight edges for interior prefixes according to sign); compare with the bad-pair condition (same left, same right, same-sign strict crossing); print any mismatch or confirmation, and keep the oracle for later stress tests.